Sounio — Epistemic Computing at the Horizon of Certainty

A systems programming language where uncertainty is a first-class citizen.

Usage: souc [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  compile       Compile a Sounio source file
  build         Build a Sounio source file to native executable (requires --features llvm)
  check         Type-check a Sounio source file without compiling
  run           Run a Sounio program using the interpreter
  jit           Run a Sounio program using JIT compilation (requires --features jit)
  repl          Start the interactive REPL
  bench         Benchmark interpreter vs JIT performance
  fmt           Format Sounio source code
  lint          Lint Sounio source code
  analyze       Analyze code for metrics and issues
  fix           Apply automatic fixes
  doc           Generate documentation for a package
  doc-book      Generate mdBook documentation
  doctest       Run documentation tests
  doc-coverage  Show documentation coverage
  info          Show information about the compiler
  test          Run tests
  benchmark     Run benchmarks
  profile       Profile a Sounio program
  debug         Debug a Sounio program
  explain       Explain an error code
  error-index   Show all error codes
  diagnostics   Diagnostics management commands
  debug-info    Generate debug information for a compiled binary
  source-map    Generate source map for compiled code
  build-system  Build project using the build system
  clean         Clean build artifacts and cache
  watch         Watch files and rebuild on changes
  serve         Start development server with live reload
  hook          Run build hooks
  target        Target management commands
  sysroot       Sysroot management commands
  ontology      Native ontology management commands
  layout        Layout synthesis commands
  locality      Locality analysis and optimization commands (Semantic-Physical Duality)
  units         Units of measure commands (dimensional analysis)
  linear        Linear/affine types commands (resource safety)
  help          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose output

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
